WHY SPARK_SRC IS NOT THE BUILD TREE

  /opt/spark-src is the pinned clone every scanner targets, and it is host-global and
  shared with concurrent clones that read it while they scan. It carries a NARROWED
  build - the provisioning built the in-scope modules only, so it holds no artifact
  for tools, examples or any connector/kafka-0-10* module, as the counts above show.
  Building the full reactor inside it would both write into a tree siblings are
  scanning and still not be this run's own build. So the build tree is a private
  clone, named in STEP 4, and SPARK_SRC is left exactly as found.
